		</span>







	
	

<header>
	
		<span class="topic" id="topic-186355946">
			<a href="//slashdot.org/index2.pl?fhfilter=themedia" onclick="return addfhfilter('themedia');">
			
				<img src="//a.fsdn.com/sd/topics/themedia_64.png" width="64" height="64" alt="The Media" title="The Media">
			
		</a>
		</span>
	
    
	<h2 class="story">
		

		

		
		

		

		

		

		<span id="title-186355946" class="story-title"> <a onclick="return toggle_fh_body_wrap_return(this);"  href="//news.slashdot.org/story/26/10/18/050211/tech-journalist-robert-x-cringely-has-died">Tech Journalist Robert X Cringely has Died</a> <span class=" no extlnk"><a class="story-sourcelnk" href="https://boingboing.net/2026/10/14/watch-triumph-of-the-nerds-the-1996-documentary-about-the-rise-of-bill-gates-and-steve-jobs.html"  title="External link - https://boingboing.net/2026/10/14/watch-triumph-of-the-nerds-the-1996-documentary-about-the-rise-of-bill-gates-and-steve-jobs.html" target="_blank"> (boingboing.net) </a></span></span>

		
		
		<!--<span class="comments commentcnt-186355946" >5</span>-->
		

		
		<!-- comment bubble -->
		
			<span class="comment-bubble"><a href="//news.slashdot.org/story/26/10/18/050211/tech-journalist-robert-x-cringely-has-died#comments" title="">5</a></span>
		
	</h2>
	<div class="details" id="details-186355946">
		<span class="story-details">
		<span class="story-views">
			<span class="sodify" onclick="firehose_set_options('color', 'red')" title="Filter Firehose to entries rated red or better"></span><span class="icon-beaker pop1 " alt="Popularity" title="Filter Firehose to entries rated red or better" onclick="firehose_set_options('color', 'red')"><span></span></span> 
		</span>
		</span>
		<span class="story-byline">
	
				
			Posted
				by 
		
		
			
				  EditorDavid
			
		
		

		
		
		<time id="fhtime-186355946" datetime="on Sunday October 18, 2026 @03:34AM">on Sunday October 18, 2026 @03:34AM</time>
		
		
			 from the <span class="dept-text">last-words</span> dept.
		
		</span>
	</div>
</header>

<div class="body" id="fhbody-186355946">
	

	
		
		<div id="text-186355946" class="p">
			
		 	
				<a href="https://boingboing.net/2026/10/14/watch-triumph-of-the-nerds-the-1996-documentary-about-the-rise-of-bill-gates-and-steve-jobs.html">BoingBoing reports</a>:
<i>Mark Stephens, <a href="https://www.cringely.com/">better known</a> under the pen name Robert X. Cringely, <a href="https://www.hillandwood.com/obituaries/Mark-Stephens?obId=49806651">died last week at 73</a>. Stephens chronicled the tech industry of the late 1980s and early 1990s &mdash; the age of Bill Gates' rise, Steve Jobs' repose, the dawn of the world wide web &mdash; and produced the famed documetary <a href="https://archive.org/details/triumph_of_the_nerds"> <em>Triumph of the Nerds</em></a>, based on his own bestselling <a href="https://amzn.to/484vnBO"> <em>Accidental Empires: How the Boys of Silicon Valley Make Their Millions, Battle Foreign Competition, and Still Can't Get a Date</em></a>.  <br> <br>

Though <a href="https://www.threads.com/@technologizer/post/DeEE9zJFXpX">not the first</a> InfoWorld columnist to write under the Cringely name, he was responsible for its <a href="https://www.wired.com/1998/12/cringely/">persona</a> and <a href="https://xent.com/FoRK-archive/summer96/0088.html">fought successfully to keep it</a> after he left the magazine in 1995.</i> <br>

"I loved the man," <a href="//slashdot.org/comments.pl?cid=66371290&amp;sid=24121340&amp;tid=384">writes</a> <a href="https://www.slashdot.org/~Darth+Technoid">Darth Technoid</a> (Slashdot reader #83,199):

<i>I first met him in the 1990s, while he was still working at InfoWorld, and we became friends immediately.  He helped me get a job or two, and he was always filled with crazy (meaning really good) ideas.<br> <br>

I'll miss him and his creativity greatly.</i> <br>

Cringely <a href="https://news.slashdot.org/story/00/09/15/0155218/interviews-come-back----with-cringelys-answers">answered questions from Slashdot's readers in 2000</a>.  And Cringely led an interesting life, as you can tell from Slashdot's January, 2020 story <a href="https://science.slashdot.org/story/20/01/25/183249/robert-cringely-attempts-an-air-launching-space-startup">Robert Cringely Attempts an Air-Launching Space Startup</a>:

<i>"How does a 67-year-old hack with three minor children recover from going blind, losing his home and business in a horrible fire (like 2,000 others, we are <em>still</em> fighting with insurance companies), while appeasing an angry crowd of Kickstarter supporters armed with pitchforks and shovels?"<br> <br>

That crowd still wants long-time tech pundit Robert X. Cringely to deliver on his Kickstarter-funded project to create custom Minecraft servers. So in <a href="https://www.cringely.com/2020/01/23/not-dead-yet-what-bob-cringely-has-been-up-to/">a new blog post this week</a>, Cringely writes that "I went looking for venture money to recapitalize <a href="https://www.cringely.com/2017/05/22/mineserver-update-not-dead-yet/">MineServer</a> and I simultaneously started a satellite launch company to fund my eventual retirement. I am not making this up..."<br> <br>

He's now found a Beverly Hills patron who wants to be a <em>co</em>-investor in the Minecraft servers, but "I will have to earn the matching money on my own, which is what I have been trying to do with my other startup, Eldorado Space."
</i> <br>

Slashdot has often linked to Cringely's commentary over the years, as <a href="https://tech.slashdot.org/story/98/06/22/0837243/the-powerpc-breakup">far back</a> <a href="https://news.slashdot.org/story/98/11/14/1025237/cringely-responds-to-dtv-show-criticism">as</a> <a href="https://linux.slashdot.org/story/98/11/08/1124242/cringely-critiques-linux-community">1998</a> and as recently as this summer. ("<a href="https://slashdot.org/story/26/06/20/0556251/tech-pundit-cringely-co-founds-startup-2brains-inc-to-solve-llm-hallucinations">Tech Pundit Cringely Co-Founds Startup '2Brains Inc' to Solve LLM Hallucinations</a>.")<ul>
<li>July, 1999: <a href="https://slashdot.org/story/99/07/01/1232205/cringelys-take-on-pirates-of-silicon-valley">Cringely's take on "Pirates of Silicon Valley"</a></li>
<li>April, 2009: <a href="https://hardware.slashdot.org/story/09/04/04/1638249/three-mile-island-memories">Three Mile Island Memories</a></li>
<li>June, 2011: <a href="https://hardware.slashdot.org/story/11/06/17/2231200/ibm-did-not-invent-the-personal-computer"> </a>IBM Did Not Invent the Personal Computer</li>
<li>March, 2019:  <a href="https://apple.slashdot.org/story/19/03/04/0546252/cringelys-final-predictions-apple-becomes-a-financial-service-and-hedge-fund">Cringely's Final Predictions: Apple Becomes a Financial Service and Hedge Fund</a></li>
<li>June, 2019: <a href="https://entertainment.slashdot.org/story/19/06/08/012239/cringely-predicts-the-end-of-broadcast-tv-within-a-decade">Cringely Predicts The End Of Broadcast TV Within A Decade</a></li>

<li>April, 2020: <a href="https://it.slashdot.org/story/20/04/04/0454207/not-just-the-death-of-it-cringely-also-predicts-layoffs-for-many-it-contractors">Not Just 'The Death of IT'. Cringely Also Predicts Layoffs For Many IT Contractors</a></li>
<li>January, 2021: <a href="https://it.slashdot.org/story/21/01/16/1745216/robert-cringley-predicted-the-death-of-it-in-2020-was-he-right">Robert Cringley Predicted 'The Death of IT' in 2020. Was He Right?</a></li>
<li>June, 2023:  <a href="https://hardware.slashdot.org/story/23/06/17/2248229/cringely-predicts-moores-law-will-continue----because-of-ai">Cringely Predicts Moore's Law Will Continue &mdash; Because of AI</a></li>
</ul><p>

But my favorite Cringely memory is <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nkCil4pPVfw"> <em>Steve Jobs: The Lost Interview</em></a>, the full 70-minute interview from 1995 that a 40-year-old Jobs gave to Cringely during filming for Triumph of the Nerds. ("And they actually sent someone to wake up the Pope....") There's various pirated copies on YouTube and <a href="https://sameerbajaj.com/jobs/">an online transcript</a>, but only 10 minutes made the broadcast &mdash; at the time Jobs was still at NeXT after his departure from Apple. But when Cringely rediscovered the videotape, the entirety of the interview was released to theaters in 2012 six months after Steve Jobs' death.  <br> <br>

Share your own memories of Robert Cringely in the comments...</p><br>
		 	
		</div>

		

		

		
	</div>
