	</article><article id="firehose-186344850" data-fhid="186344850" data-fhtype="story" class="fhitem fhitem-story article usermode thumbs grid_24">
		<span class="sd-info-block" style="display: none">
			<span class="sd-key-firehose-id">186344850</span>
			<span class="type">story</span>
			
		</span>







	
	

<header>
	
		<span class="topic" id="topic-186344850">
			<a href="//slashdot.org/index2.pl?fhfilter=privacy" onclick="return addfhfilter('privacy');">
			
				<img src="//a.fsdn.com/sd/topics/privacy_64.png" width="64" height="64" alt="Privacy" title="Privacy">
			
		</a>
		</span>
	
    
	<h2 class="story">
		

		

		
		

		

		

		

		<span id="title-186344850" class="story-title"> <a onclick="return toggle_fh_body_wrap_return(this);"  href="//yro.slashdot.org/story/26/10/17/0115242/mapquest-shows-location-of-flock-and-other-alpr-cameras">MapQuest Shows Location of Flock (and Other ALPR) Cameras</a> <span class=" no extlnk"><a class="story-sourcelnk" href="https://gizmodo.com/the-mapquest-renaissance-continues-as-the-platform-adds-flock-camera-locations-2000827015"  title="External link - https://gizmodo.com/the-mapquest-renaissance-continues-as-the-platform-adds-flock-camera-locations-2000827015" target="_blank"> (gizmodo.com) </a></span></span>

		
		
		<!--<span class="comments commentcnt-186344850" >5</span>-->
		

		
		<!-- comment bubble -->
		
			<span class="comment-bubble"><a href="//yro.slashdot.org/story/26/10/17/0115242/mapquest-shows-location-of-flock-and-other-alpr-cameras#comments" title="">5</a></span>
		
	</h2>
	<div class="details" id="details-186344850">
		<span class="story-details">
		<span class="story-views">
			<span class="sodify" onclick="firehose_set_options('color', 'red')" title="Filter Firehose to entries rated red or better"></span><span class="icon-beaker pop1 " alt="Popularity" title="Filter Firehose to entries rated red or better" onclick="firehose_set_options('color', 'red')"><span></span></span> 
		</span>
		</span>
		<span class="story-byline">
	
				
			Posted
				by 
		
		
			
				  EditorDavid
			
		
		

		
		
		<time id="fhtime-186344850" datetime="on Saturday October 17, 2026 @05:00PM">on Saturday October 17, 2026 @05:00PM</time>
		
		
			 from the <span class="dept-text">watching-the-Flock</span> dept.
		
		</span>
	</div>
</header>

<div class="body" id="fhbody-186344850">
	

	
		
		<div id="text-186344850" class="p">
			
		 	
				MapQuest creates a new layer (that can be toggled on and off), <a href="https://gizmodo.com/the-mapquest-renaissance-continues-as-the-platform-adds-flock-camera-locations-2000827015">Gizmodo reports</a>:


<i>After promising not to comply with the Trump administration's "Lake America" gimmick, the platform announced a new "Surveillance Layer" that displays the locations of automated license plate readers (ALPRs), including those from Flock Safety.   Per MapQuest, its new tool will identify the locations of known outdoor surveillance cameras and plate readers from Motorola Solutions (Vigilant), Genetec, Axis Communications, Axon, Leonardo (ELSAG), Neology, Rekor, PlateSmart, Ubicquia, Verkada, and others.<br> <br>

While the company didn't specify how it sources its data, it appears to be similar to the <a href="https://maps.deflock.org/?lat=39.8283&amp;lng=-98.5795&amp;zoom=4.00">data amassed by DeFlock</a>, which maintains a user-submitted map of ALPR camera locations. MapQuest may be sourcing the information from DeFlock and the OpenStreetMap project.</i> <br>

Engadget <a href="https://www.engadget.com/2288729/mapquest-will-now-show-you-where-flock-cameras-are-in-your-neighborhood/">notes that MapQuest also recently added</a> "useful, long-overdue features like Android Auto support and public transit directions."<br>
		 	
		</div>

		

		

		
	</div>
	<aside class="novote">
		
	</aside>
	
	  	

		
		<footer class="clearfix meta article-foot">
			<div class="story-controls">
				
                    
					
				
			</div>
			
				
				<div class="story-tags">
					<span class="tright tags"><menu type="toolbar" class="edit-bar">
		<span id="tagbar-186344850" class="tag-bar none">
			
		</span>
		
